 "headline": "Both sides answered all 38 comparable cases with no failures and scored 20/20 on the 20 mechanically labelled questions. Median round trip was 0.336 s local fast, 0.384 s local accuracy, and 0.326 s hosted; hosted p90 of 0.511 s beat local p90 of 0.901 s. The eight-read accuracy profile changed no answer on this suite while adding about 14 percent to median latency, so the default stays fast.",
 "limitations": [
  "20/20 on both sides is a weak signal. Only 6 of the 20 labelled questions have a single correct key; the other 14 accept either of two keys, so the ceiling is easy to reach and this suite does not separate the two systems on quality.",
  "Hosted answers are not ground truth. They are an agreement reference. The labels are mechanical, derived from each case's own state, not human annotation.",
  "Retrieval metrics are undefined here. nDCG and MRR need a ranked candidate list against relevance judgments, and no case in this suite ranks a list, so neither is reported rather than reported as a placeholder.",
  "The single top-choice disagreement is probe/score_three_levels. Hosted scored 1.98 of 2 and local scored about 1.02, on a state whose text reads as a third escalation. Hosted's reading is the more plausible one.",
  "The first case of every local run carries warm-up. checkout/struggling took 4.005 s on the fast run and 2.026 s on the accuracy run, against medians near 0.34 s and 0.38 s, which is why medians and p90 are reported rather than a mean.",
  "One paired run per profile, 38 cases, one machine, one residential network, one day. No repeated trials, so no confidence interval is claimed on any latency figure.",
  "Two payloads that hosted Jev answered are rejected by the local strict schema: a structured Noul criteria object and null Choice descriptions. They are counted as hosted-only inputs and excluded from the answer comparison, because there is no local answer to compare.",
  "Held-out evaluation remains unfinished. The development-set seed sweep in the accuracy study is not a held-out result, and no accuracy winner is claimed from it."
 ],
